 the epic, settled siblings, or shipped code","The epic's own ADR acceptance criterion prescribes no 'two of three' anchor — the phrase is introduced only by this child plan"],"finding":"The AC directs the ADR body to record a 'reproduce-before-admit threshold' with the literal anchor grep -c \"two of three\", but no settled sibling or shipped code implements a two-of-three reproduction threshold — the real rule is a same-material_fingerprint reproduction consensus (>=2 equal-fingerprint reviews) plus a single reproduce-or-withhold admission bar, so the anchor names a decision that does not exist.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f0b1a045f50c76bde","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria, first bullet — anchor 'the reproduce-before-admit threshold (grep -c \"two of three\")'; and Approach, 'the reproduce-before-admit rule and its two-of-three threshold'","norm_id":"n96f6597e0116a1ab","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementer writes the ADR to satisfy grep -c \"two of three\" and invents a 2-of-3 threshold the code does not implement — the ADR (whose purpose is to record the real protocol) documents a fiction a future contributor will trust","Implementer notices the code has no 2-of-3 rule and drops/renames the anchor, diverging from the AC as written"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Change the AC anchor from grep -c \"two of three\" to a phrase the settled decision uses — e.g. grep -c \"reproduction consensus\" (matching fixture_selection.py's 'reproduction_consensus' signal / >=2 equal-fingerprint reviews) — and reword the Approach line 'its two-of-three threshold' to 'its same-fingerprint reproduction-consensus rule and the reproduce-before-admit bar.'","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked